course: dictionary
lesson: 5977
title: Maybe: perhaps, a soft suggestion, or not sure
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Maybe is a small word with a big job. Most often it means perhaps: it might be true, or it might not, and you are not sure. «The bus might be late, maybe ten minutes.» The writer is guessing here, not stating a fact.
explain: Maybe can also make a suggestion gentle and polite. «Maybe we could share the cake.» The speaker is not giving an order. They offer an idea and leave room for you to say no. Look at the words around maybe to tell which meaning it has.
explain: Maybe can also be a noun, as in «a maybe», meaning an answer that is neither yes nor no. This use is informal, so you will hear it more in chat and speech than in formal writing. Context shows whether maybe is a guess, a soft suggestion, or an answer.
explain: In maths and science, maybe often marks an idea you have not yet proved. Treat it as a guess to check. Say maybe, then test the idea before you believe it. Guess and check is a good habit.
fact: Maybe means perhaps: it might be true, or it might not.
fact: «Maybe» can soften a suggestion, as in «Maybe we could share.»
fact: As a noun, «a maybe» is an answer that is neither yes nor no (informal).
fact: In a story, «maybe» can show that a character is not sure, as in «I shall sit here till tomorrow—or next day, maybe.»
fact: Useful phrases: «maybe not», «maybe later», «maybe so».
exercise: «The bus might be late, maybe ten minutes.» What does maybe mean here? | *Perhaps, it might be true or might not | Yesterday | Very loudly | Definitely, it is certain
exercise: Ava asks, «Maybe we could share the cake?» What is Ava doing? | Asking the time | Stating a fact about cake | Giving a loud order | *Making a soft, polite suggestion
exercise: Sam says, «Maybe later,» because he cannot decide right now. What does maybe later suggest? | *Not now, possibly another time | The name of a game | Never, ever again | Right now, immediately
test: «It was a maybe, neither yes nor no.» As a noun, what is a maybe? | A kind of bird | A loud noise | A question about the weather | *An answer that is neither yes nor no
test: Mia says, «Maybe not,» after thinking. What does maybe not suggest? | A spelling mistake | *Possibly no, she is slightly changing her mind | Definitely yes | The word not is missing
exam: In «I shall sit here till tomorrow—or next day, maybe.», what does maybe show about the speaker? | They are certain of the day | *They are not sure of the exact day | They are asleep | They are shouting
